en:
//　矢の如く<RUBY text='・'>俺</RUBY>の前を過ぎていった光陰は――
//　ここから急に、精彩を失う。
  Here, the narrative that has unfolded before me loses clarity and focus.

//　<RUBY text='おれの'>三世</RUBY>村正は、これ以降の事変の殆どを自分の眼では
//見なかったのだろう。
//　幾つかの短い映像と伝聞で得たらしき情報とがひと
//まとめに、俺の認識上を滑ってゆく。
  The events that followed, <I>my</I>㉑Muramasa did not witness with her own eyes. They are revealed to me as she learned of them, through brief images and secondhand accounts.

//　遂に完成した始祖村正そして二世村正、この二領の
//劒冑は性能において頂点へ達していたのは無論だが、
//加えて異常な特質を備えてもいた。
//　それは千子村正だけのものであり、二つあった。
  Old Muramasa and his daughter went to their forge, and the tsurugi that emerged were indeed exceptional in strength and ability. In addition, they possessed two powers―some might call them curses―that were unique to their line.


//　一つは〝善悪相殺〟の戒律である。
//　対敵を一人殺したなら味方も一人。悪しき者を一人
//殺したなら善き者も一人。憎む者を一人殺したなら、
//愛する者もまた一人、殺さねばならない。
  First was the Law of Balance.

  One good for one evil.<K>
  One friend for one enemy.<K>
  One beloved for one despised.

  This was the price that Muramasa demanded of its masters.

//　村正と結縁した武者はこの掟を背負う。
//　己の善のみ盲信し、敵の善は悪と看做して排除する、
//その〝独善〟を力で押し通すことを、村正という劒冑
//は許さないのだ。
  Thus no musha who joined with a tsurugi of their line would ever be able to call his battle "just," nor would he be able to wield his might freely. For though Muramasa's power was second to none, to slay an enemy in service of his dream would be to himself become that dream's downfall.

  This was the first step toward eliminating man's self-righteousness, the ability to judge oneself good and one's enemy evil that lay at the heart of all conflict.


//　衆に卓抜する村正の<RUBY text='ちから'>暴威</RUBY>で望みを遂げようとすれば、
//己の手でその望みを打ち砕く結末に至る。
//　村正武者は最強にして、誰よりも武力の行使を自重
//する人物にならざるを得ないであろう。

//　もう一つは〝精神同調〟の<RUBY text='わざ'>能</RUBY>である。
//　村正は『波』を放散し、周囲の人間の精神に仕手の
//それを重ねることができるのだ。
  The second step, and the second power, was that of Synchronization. The Muramasa tsurugi could emit invisible "waves," waves that imposed their master's state of mind upon any human within their area of effect.

//　仕手の精神に浸透した善悪相殺の戒律も写される。
//　一軍全体を、村正の思想に沿う集団へと変貌せしめ
//られるのである。
  The Law of Balance would thus be transmitted to the musha's compatriots, forcing an entire army to embody the truth of war.

//　武者ならば甲鉄の防護力をもって『波』の力に抵抗
//するも可能だが……
//　村正はこの能力の変形として『卵』を生成する事で、
//遂には武者の精神をも逃さぬのだった。
  Even musha were not safe from Synchronization. Though they were shielded from the waves by their enchanted armor, Muramasa could still infect their tsurugi with "eggs," concentrations of corrupting energy that would grow within the tsurugi's armor and, upon "hatching," transform it into a relay for Muramasa's power.

  The new tsurugi's first victim would be its own pilot.

//『卵』は劒冑に移植されると内部で生育、やがて孵化
//し、劒冑を『波』の<RUBY text='・・・'>中継点</RUBY>に造り替える。
//　新たに発散される『波』の影響を第一に受けるのは、
//最も近くにいる者、つまりその劒冑の仕手である……。

//　村正の仕手に利己心あらば、この〝精神同調〟能力
//を味方の軍に対して使おうとは思わないであろう。
//　敵軍に対して用い、戦意を奪おうとする筈である。
  That said, there was no reason to believe that Muramasa's master would brainwash his own men with its power. A sensible musha would use it to disable only his enemy's forces, thereby ensuring victory.

//　しかし、だからこそ始祖村正は劒冑を二領用意して、
//対立する両陣営に与えたのだ。
//　双方の村正武者が敵に対して〝精神同調〟を行使し
//合えば、一方だけが優勢になるような事態は起きない。
  Which was, of course, precisely the reason old Muramasa and his daughter forged㉓<I>two</I> tsurugi, one for each side of the conflict. If each used Synchronization against the other, then the Law of Balance would rule the entire battlefield.

//　戦場は<RUBY text='あまね'>遍</RUBY>く〝善悪相殺〟の戒律に支配される。

//　完璧――そう言って良かった。
//　始祖村正が劒冑に懸けた理想は、これ以上はないと
//いう形で結実した。
  It was perfect. Old Muramasa's plan had left no room for error, no chance that something might prevent the realization of his dream.

//　この劒冑は必ずや世に平和をもたらす。
//　長きに渡り続いた南北朝の乱を、穏健に終息させる。
  These tsurugi would bring peace to Yamato. The long war between North and South would come to a graceful end.

//　始祖村正はそう信じた。
//　<RUBY text='むすめ'>二世村正</RUBY>も信じ、<RUBY text='まご'>三世村正</RUBY>も疑わなかった。
  So old Muramasa believed, so his daughter believed, and so even his granddaughter did not doubt.

//　…………が。
//　
//　事実はそうならなかったことを、後世に生きる俺は
//知っている。
  That things did not proceed as they hoped... is something we who possess the benefit of hindsight know all too well.

//　南北朝の時代は――
//　その最後に未曾有の殲滅戦争を巻き起こし、わずか
//一年で当時の全人口の一割とも二割以上とも云われる
//死者を出して、閉幕へ至るのだ。
  History tells that the Nanbokucho War ended in absolute chaos, a horrifying bloodbath that claimed the lives of, experts estimate, as much as twenty percent of the total population of Yamato.

//　災厄の劒冑。
//　三代で絶えた妖甲の一門、千子右衛門尉村正の<RUBY text='な'>銘</RUBY>を
//歴史に刻んで。
  Thus the line of Sengo Muramasa came to be reviled as cursed, insane, and though they vanished after only three generations, the world will forever remember them as the demon armors of legend.
